From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(resource-packs): read complete server archives

Some server archives put their manifest and assets beneath one pack directory. Select that root only when unambiguous, prefer an existing root manifest, and normalize repeated Windows separators before resolving assets. Minehut and Geyser recordings exercise those layouts.

Enchanted advertises a valid 1,251,017-byte ZIP with 58 stored files using data descriptors. ZipInputStream rejects that layout. Read the central directory through the existing Commons Compress dependency and an in-memory seekable channel, preserving physical entry order, size checks, and CRC verification. This also avoids scanning for descriptor signatures inside nested ZIP payloads.

Archive regressions cover nested roots, root preference, Windows paths, stored descriptors with embedded ZIP signatures, and corrupted entry data. The private Enchanted download reproduces the old failure and loads all 58 files with this reader. Commons documents the seekable reader behavior at https://commons.apache.org/proper/commons-compress/zip .
